netfilter: nft_set_pipapo: prevent overflow in lookup table allocation

jira KERNEL-1646
cve CVE-2025-38162
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8
commit-author Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
commit 4c5c6aa9967dbe55bd017bb509885928d0f31206
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.51.1.el9_8/4c5c6aa9.failed

When calculating the lookup table size, ensure the following
multiplication does not overflow:

- desc->field_len[] maximum value is U8_MAX multiplied by
  NFT_PIPAPO_GROUPS_PER_BYTE(f) that can be 2, worst case.
- NFT_PIPAPO_BUCKETS(f->bb) is 2^8, worst case.
- sizeof(unsigned long), from sizeof(*f->lt), lt in
  struct nft_pipapo_field.

Then, use check_mul_overflow() to multiply by bucket size and then use
check_add_overflow() to the alignment for avx2 (if needed). Finally, add
lt_size_check_overflow() helper and use it to consolidate this.

While at it, replace leftover allocation using the GFP_KERNEL to
GFP_KERNEL_ACCOUNT for consistency, in pipapo_resize().

Fixes: 3c4287f62044 ("nf_tables: Add set type for arbitrary concatenation of ranges")
	Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
	Reviewed-by: Stefano Brivio <sbrivio@redhat.com>
	Signed-off-by: Pablo Neira Ayuso <pablo@netfilter.org>
(cherry picked from commit 4c5c6aa9967dbe55bd017bb509885928d0f31206)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	net/netfilter/nft_set_pipapo.c
